            "findings": [
              {
                "id": "R1-001",
                "lens": "risk",
                "location": "CHANGELOG.md:17",
                "severity": "SUGGESTION",
                "claim": "The changelog entry says the CI step 'Committed actuals records validate' still calls the validator without --repo and fails until patched. This candidate's own .github/workflows/ci.yml change already applies that patch, so the sentence is stale. This is a documentation inaccuracy, not a security risk.",
                "proof_refs": [
                  "CHANGELOG.md:17",
                  ".github/workflows/ci.yml:235-257"
                ]
              }
            ],
            "evidence": [
              "Reviewed all 11 changed paths for security, data exposure, unsafe input handling and dependency risk.",
              "The validator takes --repo and change_name from the caller and the record. The change name is passed to app.CountLenses, which the patch notes say refuses any name that is not one safe path segment, and it reads only files named like results. Stat, read and parse failures all exit non-zero (exit 7 for unreadable results). I found no reachable traversal or fail-open path in the visible code.",
              "The go.mod change adds a local replace to ../../engine and no third-party module, so it adds no dependency-vulnerability surface.",
              "The CI change runs jq 'del(.review_lens_count)' on committed fixtures into a RUNNER_TEMP file, with quoted variables and no untrusted input. The member is removed only for the committed legacy fixture, which the Go test pins as refused by design, so it adds no exploitable weakening.",
              "Missing --repo now exits 2 and an unreadable repository or result exits 7, so the check refuses instead of passing when it cannot run."
            ]
          }
        }
